-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 39 Rule 2 -- application for registration`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The three kinds of instrument that can be registered, each "called in this Order" by a short name.
DECLARE `o 39 r 2 kind of instrument` IS ONE OF
    `o 39 r 2(a) a Commitment`
    `o 39 r 2(b) a Direction`
    `o 39 r 2(c) a Decision`
    `o 39 r 2 not one of the three kinds`

-- FORK F39.2 | "(called in this Order a Commitment)", "(a Direction)", "(a Decision)": "called" is neither "means" nor "only", the two words that make a definition say no in its own words, so these are labels and the three descriptions do not close the list; an instrument that fits none of them (a direction made under a section other than 58A, 67 or 69, for example) is NOTHING (the text at r 2(b) does not point the other way: it lists what the application is made for and names the label in a bracket) | JUST FALSE (read as stipulative definitions: the list is closed, and anything else is not an instrument of this Order)
-- src:5516 | Application for registration (O. 39, r. 2)
-- src:5517 | 2. An application for the registration in the District Court of — ( a )
-- src:5518 | any commitment accepted by the Competition and Consumer Commission of Singapore under section 60A (called in this Order a Commitment);
-- src:5519 | ( b )
-- src:5520 | any direction made by the Competition and Consumer Commission of Singapore pursuant to section 58A, 67 or 69 (called in this Order a Direction); or
-- src:5521 | ( c )
-- src:5522 | any decision made by the Competition Appeal Board (called in this Order a Decision),
-- src:5523 | must be made by originating application without notice.
@ref O 39 r 2 (src:5516-5523)
GIVEN `it is a commitment accepted by the Competition and Consumer Commission of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a direction made by the Competition and Consumer Commission of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a decision made by the Competition Appeal Board` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the section under which the Commission accepted or made it` IS A STRING
GIVETH A `o 39 r 2 kind of instrument`
`o 39 r 2 the kind of instrument` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `it is a commitment accepted by the Competition and Consumer Commission of Singapore` AND `the section under which the Commission accepted or made it` EQUALS "60A"
           THEN `o 39 r 2(a) a Commitment`
           IF `it is a direction made by the Competition and Consumer Commission of Singapore` AND elem `the section under which the Commission accepted or made it` (LIST "58A", "67", "69")
           THEN `o 39 r 2(b) a Direction`
           IF `it is a decision made by the Competition Appeal Board`
           THEN `o 39 r 2(c) a Decision`
           OTHERWISE `o 39 r 2 not one of the three kinds` -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "called in this Order" names only the three described instruments and does not say "means"

-- Where and how the application is made.
DECLARE `o 39 r 2 how the application is made` IS ONE OF
    `o 39 r 2 by originating application without notice`
    `o 39 r 2 by originating application with notice`
    `o 39 r 2 by summons`
    `o 39 r 2 in some other way`

-- "An application for the registration in the District Court of ... must be made by originating application without notice."
-- FORK QB | bare "must be made": made another way | NOTHING | JUST FALSE for the compliance question
-- src:5516 | Application for registration (O. 39, r. 2)
-- src:5517 | 2. An application for the registration in the District Court of — ( a )
-- src:5518 | any commitment accepted by the Competition and Consumer Commission of Singapore under section 60A (called in this Order a Commitment);
-- src:5519 | ( b )
-- src:5520 | any direction made by the Competition and Consumer Commission of Singapore pursuant to section 58A, 67 or 69 (called in this Order a Direction); or
-- src:5521 | ( c )
-- src:5522 | any decision made by the Competition Appeal Board (called in this Order a Decision),
-- src:5523 | must be made by originating application without notice.
@ref O 39 r 2 (src:5516-5523)
GIVEN kind IS A `o 39 r 2 kind of instrument`
      `the application is for registration in the District Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      how IS A `o 39 r 2 how the application is made`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 39 r 2 the application for registration is made as the Rule requires` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `the application is for registration in the District Court`)
           THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An application for the registration in the District Court"
           IF kind EQUALS `o 39 r 2 not one of the three kinds`
           THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Rule speaks only of a Commitment, a Direction or a Decision
           IF how EQUALS `o 39 r 2 by originating application without notice`
           THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must be made" (QB); Rule 2 does not say what follows an application made another way

