-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 39 Rule 8 -- endorsement of service`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

`o 39 r 8(1) the period for endorsing the notice` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 3
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- Rule 8(1): "Within 3 days after service of the notice of registration or within such longer period as the Court may,
-- in special circumstances, allow, the notice or a copy of the notice must be endorsed by the person who served it with
-- the day of the week and date on which it was served."  The last day is Order 3, Rule 3's; a longer period the Court
-- has allowed replaces it.  A period the text fixes in its own words: after it, JUST FALSE.
-- src:5562 | 8. —(1) Within 3 days after service of the notice of registration or within such longer period as the Court may, in special circumstances, allow, the notice or a copy of the notice must be endorsed by the person who served it with the day of the week and date on which it was served. (2) If the notice is not so endorsed within the period mentioned in paragraph (1), the person seeking to enforce the Commitment, Direction or Decision may not apply for an enforcement order to enforce the Commitment, Direction or Decision to which the notice relates without the permission of the Court.
@ref O 39 r 8(1) (src:5562)
GIVEN `the date the notice was endorsed` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the longer period the Court has allowed in special circumstances` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 39 r 8(1) the notice is endorsed in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last day of the longer period the Court has allowed in special circumstances`
    WHEN JUST longer THEN
        IF `the date the notice was endorsed` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` OR `the date the notice was endorsed` AT MOST longer
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Within 3 days after service of the notice of registration or within such longer period as the Court may, in special circumstances, allow"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF `the date the notice was endorsed` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Within 3 days after service of the notice of registration"

-- The duty as a regulative rule: the person who served the notice endorses it within 3 days.  The text names no
-- consequence in this paragraph (paragraph (2) restricts the enforcing party), so the default consequence of a lapsed
-- MUST is the language's, not the Rules'.
DECLARE `o 39 r 8(1) party` IS ONE OF
    `o 39 r 8(1) the person who served the notice`

DECLARE `o 39 r 8(1) action` IS ONE OF
    `o 39 r 8(1) endorse the notice with the day of the week and date of service`

-- src:5562 | 8. —(1) Within 3 days after service of the notice of registration or within such longer period as the Court may, in special circumstances, allow, the notice or a copy of the notice must be endorsed by the person who served it with the day of the week and date on which it was served. (2) If the notice is not so endorsed within the period mentioned in paragraph (1), the person seeking to enforce the Commitment, Direction or Decision may not apply for an enforcement order to enforce the Commitment, Direction or Decision to which the notice relates without the permission of the Court.
@ref O 39 r 8(1) (src:5562)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `o 39 r 8(1) party` `o 39 r 8(1) action`
`o 39 r 8(1) the duty to endorse the notice` MEANS
    PARTY `o 39 r 8(1) the person who served the notice`
    MUST `o 39 r 8(1) endorse the notice with the day of the week and date of service`
    WITHIN 3

